To all those who do not beleive that there can be more than one of the 
Named weapons:

Playing a Valkyrie (who gets a long sword +1 free) I made it up to 5th level
(easy) and quickly paced it over to the nearest fountain [saved the game]
and dipped it in.  What did I get?

A water demon. (OOPS).

Granted a wish (cunning), so I wished for Stormbringer.  Got it.

[saved]

There was still a fountain, so kept dipping the long sword.  Fountain dried up.

Ho Hum.

Went downstairs, found a fountain (OK so it was a lucky game I suppose) dipped
long sword in a few times.  Murky hand an' all.  Two named weapons.

That shows them who think that two named weapons are not possible to get a 
thing or two.

[Saved the game for future reference]

Promptly died of starvation.

[Restored]

Promptly died of starvation.

[Restored]

Went downstairs, found an altar (Chaotic), found a jaguar, made a jaguar corpse
(easy with Stormy).  Offered it at the altar, got a second Stormbringer.

Got killed by a band of orcs.  (oops)

[Restored]

Found another bones level of mine with a (admittedly cursed) Stormy and
Excalibur.  Left them alone.  Got killed by a hobbit who found them lying
around.  Believe me they worked.

So, it seems that it is possible (though extermely useless) to have multiple
Named weapons.  (I was surprised myself actually).

Well hope I haven't bored you to tears.

Timmo.


